sieve-filter-v2
; Every note in one key: its pitch class belongs to the scale on the tonic; rests always pass.
; The built-in key-v1 as data, with its scale as a choice, so a stack of melody plugins that
; includes the key still counts and ranks (a stack mixing plugins with a built-in filter may not).
; key-data-v1 is the same rule for the major scale only, and stays as it was.
;
; A pitch's class above the tonic is (LOW + p - 1 - tonic) mod 12, worked out once for each pitch
; by a for loop of one pass; the scales are key-v1's: major 0 2 4 5 7 9 11, minor 0 2 3 5 7 8 10,
; harmonic minor 0 2 3 5 7 8 11, major pentatonic 0 2 4 7 9, minor pentatonic 0 3 5 7 10, blues
; 0 3 5 6 7 10.
id        key-data
version   2
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes*
describe  Every note is in the key: its pitch class is in the scale on the tonic. Rests always pass.
param     tonic  choice C C,C#,D,D#,E,F,F#,G,G#,A,A#,B the key's first note
param     scale  choice major major,minor,harmonic-minor,major-pentatonic,minor-pentatonic,blues the scale's notes

states    1
start     0
accept    0
for d 0 {DURATIONS - 1}
  t 0 @{d} 0
  for p 1 {PITCHES}
    for r {(LOW + p - 1 + 12 - tonic) % 12} {(LOW + p - 1 + 12 - tonic) % 12}
      if {(scale == 0 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 4 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 9 || r == 11)) || (scale == 1 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 8 || r == 10)) || (scale == 2 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 8 || r == 11)) || (scale == 3 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 4 || r == 7 || r == 9)) || (scale == 4 && (r == 0 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 10)) || (scale == 5 && (r == 0 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 6 || r == 7 || r == 10))}
        t 0 @{p * DURATIONS + d} 0
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
